From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: move AKM_SUITE_SAE out of the APCLI guard

AKM_SUITE_SAE was defined inside #ifdef APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT, but
CFG80211OS_MloExternalAuthRequest() is built for every DOT11_EHT_BE target and
uses the constant, so an AP-only build without the APCLI supplicant failed with
"'AKM_SUITE_SAE' undeclared". Hoist the definition above both guards.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_util.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/cfg80211/cfg80211_util.c
@@ -921,8 +921,17 @@
 	return pChCtrl->ChListNum;
 }
 
-#ifdef APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT
+/*
+ * 0x08ac0f00 is the byte-swapped OUI/type pair hostapd expects here.  The
+ * define used to live inside the APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT block, but
+ * CFG80211OS_MloExternalAuthRequest() is built for every DOT11_EHT_BE target
+ * and needs it too, so keep it outside of both feature guards.
+ */
+#ifndef AKM_SUITE_SAE
 #define AKM_SUITE_SAE 0x08ac0f00
+#endif
+
+#ifdef APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT
 int CFG80211OS_ExternalAuthRequest(PSTA_ADMIN_CONFIG pStaCfg)
 {
 	int ret, len;
